This time I decided to go through the code to figure out what the exact
chances of an L monster getting Magicbane really are.  It's only arch
liches that have any chance at all.  For that matter only master liches
or arch liches have any chance of getting an athame.

Here is my commentary in makemon.c in the sources in 3.4.3:

	    case S_LICH:
No lich weaker than master lich gets an initial weapon.

		if (ptr == &mons[PM_MASTER_LICH] && !rn2(13))
			(void)mongets(mtmp, (rn2(7) ? ATHAME : WAN_NOTHING));

One in 13 master liches get a weapon. Six in 7 of those weapons are
athames. None are ever artifacts.

		else if (ptr == &mons[PM_ARCH_LICH] && !rn2(3)) {
			otmp = mksobj(rn2(3) ? ATHAME : QUARTERSTAFF,
				      TRUE, rn2(13) ? FALSE : TRUE);

One in 3 arch liches get a weapon.  Two in 3 of those weapons are
athames.  So 2 in 9 arch liches get an athame.  One in 13 of those
athames tries to be an artifact if Magicbane does not exist yet. That's
2 in 117 arch liches tries to get Magicbane.

			if (otmp->spe < 2) otmp->spe = rnd(3);
			if (!rn2(4)) otmp->oerodeproof = 1;
			(void) mpickobj(mtmp, otmp);
		}
		break;

Arch liches also get better enchanted athames and a 1 in 4 chance of it
being rustproof.  A fireproof +2 quarterstaff is not a bad thing to
have.

Looking at mkobj.c it's worse than 2 in 117, though:

		if (artif && !rn2(20))
		    otmp = mk_artifact(otmp, (aligntyp)A_NONE);

Only 1 in 20 attempts at an artifact actually get one.  So it's not 2 in
117 master liches that actually get Magicbane.  It's 2 in 2340.  There
is also a check in artifact.c to make sure it does not exist yet.

Fight all 120 master liches to extinction and you have a few percent
chance of getting Magicbane.  Clearly a rare event.  As we all know rare
events seem to happen all the time to some poster or other.  Just not to
me.  Unless it's something bad.  Sigh.  Dying in combat with an arch
lich is not a rare event for me.  It's why I would rather blessed
genocide L than try to get Magicbane this way.


